1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,050
Section 1

2
00:00:02,050 --> 00:00:02,674
ANDREW:

3
00:00:02,674 --> 00:00:04,688
Good morning, Clare House Hotel.

4
00:00:04,688 --> 00:00:06,063
Andre speaking.

5
00:00:06,063 --> 00:00:08,070
I'm the Events Manager.

6
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:08,554
SAM:

7
00:00:08,554 --> 00:00:10,005
Good morning, Andrew.

8
00:00:10,005 --> 00:00:11,456
My name's Samantha.

9
00:00:11,456 --> 00:00:16,292
I'm arranging a party for my parents' fiftieth wedding anniversary,

10
00:00:16,292 --> 00:00:22,580
and I'm ringing to ask about hiring a room some time next September.

11
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:27,900
Also my parents and several of the guests will need accommodation.

12
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:28,316
ANDREW:

13
00:00:28,316 --> 00:00:32,060
OK, I'm sure we can help you with that.

14
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:36,220
Will you be having a sit-down meal or a buffet?

15
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:37,020
SAM:

16
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:39,420
Probably a sit-down.

17
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:39,819
ANDREW:

18
00:00:39,819 --> 00:00:43,410
And do you know how many people there'll be?

19
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:44,082
SAM:

20
00:00:44,082 --> 00:00:46,770
Around eighty, I think.

21
00:00:46,770 --> 00:00:47,208
ANDREW:

22
00:00:47,208 --> 00:00:51,582
Well we have two rooms that can hold that number.

23
00:00:51,582 --> 00:00:53,770
One is the Adelphi Room.

24
00:00:53,770 --> 00:00:55,520
That can seat eighty-five,

25
00:00:55,520 --> 00:01:00,770
or hold over a hundred if people are standing for a buffet.

26
00:01:00,770 --> 00:01:01,830
SAM:

27
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:02,890
Right.

28
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:03,297
ANDREW:

29
00:01:03,297 --> 00:01:08,995
If you have live music, there's room for four or five musicians in the

30
00:01:08,995 --> 00:01:10,623
gallery overlooking the room.

31
00:01:10,623 --> 00:01:16,321
Our guests usually appreciate the fact that the music can be loud enough for

32
00:01:16,321 --> 00:01:16,728
dancing,

33
00:01:16,728 --> 00:01:19,170
but not too loud for conversation.

34
00:01:19,170 --> 00:01:19,609
SAM:

35
00:01:19,609 --> 00:01:24,000
Yes, I really don't like it when you can't talk.

36
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:24,441
ANDREW:

37
00:01:24,441 --> 00:01:24,882
Exactly.

38
00:01:24,882 --> 00:01:29,734
Now the Adelphi Room is at the back of the hotel,

39
00:01:29,734 --> 00:01:34,144
and there are French windows leading out onto the terrace.

40
00:01:34,144 --> 00:01:40,319
This has a beautiful display of pots of roses at that time of the

41
00:01:40,319 --> 00:01:40,760
year.

42
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:41,250
SAM:

43
00:01:41,250 --> 00:01:43,700
Which direction does it face?

44
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:44,154
ANDREW:

45
00:01:44,154 --> 00:01:44,607
Southwest,

46
00:01:44,607 --> 00:01:50,049
so that side of the hotel gets the sun in the afternoon

47
00:01:50,049 --> 00:01:51,410
and early evening.

48
00:01:51,410 --> 00:01:52,223
SAM:

49
00:01:52,223 --> 00:01:53,850
very nice.

50
00:01:53,850 --> 00:01:54,231
ANDREW:

51
00:01:54,231 --> 00:01:59,558
From the terrace you can see the area of trees within the grounds of

52
00:01:59,558 --> 00:02:00,319
the hotel,

53
00:02:00,319 --> 00:02:05,646
or you can stroll through there to the river -that's on the far side,

54
00:02:05,646 --> 00:02:08,310
so it isn't visible from the hotel.

55
00:02:08,310 --> 00:02:09,485
SAM:

56
00:02:09,485 --> 00:02:10,660
OK.

57
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:11,061
ANDREW:

58
00:02:11,061 --> 00:02:13,867
Then another option is the Carlton Room.

59
00:02:13,867 --> 00:02:18,276
This is a bit bigger-it can hold up to a hundred

60
00:02:18,276 --> 00:02:22,686
and ten people -and it has the advantage of a stage,

61
00:02:22,686 --> 00:02:25,892
which is useful if you have any entertainment,

62
00:02:25,892 --> 00:02:29,500
or indeed a small band can fit onto it.

63
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:29,938
SAM:

64
00:02:29,938 --> 00:02:33,440
And can you go outside from the room?

65
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:33,877
ANDREW:

66
00:02:33,877 --> 00:02:37,811
No, the Carlton Room is on the first floor,

67
00:02:37,811 --> 00:02:42,620
but on one side the windows look out onto the lake.

68
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:43,099
SAM:

69
00:02:43,099 --> 00:02:43,578
Lovely.

70
00:02:43,578 --> 00:02:47,890
I think either of those rooms would be suitable.

71
00:02:47,890 --> 00:02:48,239
ANDREW:

72
00:02:48,239 --> 00:02:52,770
Can I tell you about some of the options we offer in addition?

73
00:02:52,770 --> 00:02:53,513
SAM:

74
00:02:53,513 --> 00:02:55,000
Please do.

75
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:55,394
ANDREW:

76
00:02:55,394 --> 00:03:00,905
As well as a meal, you can have an MC, a Master of Ceremonies,

77
00:03:00,905 --> 00:03:03,660
who'll be with you throughout the party.

78
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:04,074
SAM:

79
00:03:04,074 --> 00:03:06,555
What exactly is the MC's function?

80
00:03:06,555 --> 00:03:12,346
I suppose they make a speech during the meal if we need one, do

81
00:03:12,346 --> 00:03:12,760
they?

82
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:13,192
ANDREW:

83
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:14,057
That's right.

84
00:03:14,057 --> 00:03:17,515
All our MCs are trained as public speakers,

85
00:03:17,515 --> 00:03:23,135
so they can easily get people's attention - many guests are glad to have

86
00:03:23,135 --> 00:03:27,026
someone who can make themselves heard above the chatter!

87
00:03:27,026 --> 00:03:32,646
And they're also your support - if anything goes wrong, the MC will deal

88
00:03:32,646 --> 00:03:33,511
with it,

89
00:03:33,511 --> 00:03:35,240
so you can relax.

90
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:35,762
SAM:

91
00:03:35,762 --> 00:03:36,284
Great!

92
00:03:36,284 --> 00:03:39,938
I'll need to ask you about food,

93
00:03:39,938 --> 00:03:43,592
but something else that's important is accommodation.

94
00:03:43,592 --> 00:03:47,246
You obviously have rooms in the hotel,

95
00:03:47,246 --> 00:03:53,510
but do you also have any other accommodation, like cabins for example?

96
00:03:53,510 --> 00:03:54,017
ANDREW:

97
00:03:54,017 --> 00:03:58,584
Yes, there are five in the grounds, all self-contained.

98
00:03:58,584 --> 00:04:05,688
They each sleep two to four people and have their own living room, bathroom

99
00:04:05,688 --> 00:04:07,210
and small kitchen.

100
00:04:07,210 --> 00:04:07,691
SAM:

101
00:04:07,691 --> 00:04:11,060
That sounds perfect for what we'll need.

102
00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:11,502
SAM:

103
00:04:11,502 --> 00:04:14,594
Now you have various facilities, don't you?

104
00:04:14,594 --> 00:04:19,453
Are they all included in the price of hiring the room?

105
00:04:19,453 --> 00:04:21,220
The pool, for instance.

106
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:21,663
ANDREW:

107
00:04:21,663 --> 00:04:24,761
Normally you'd be able to use it,

108
00:04:24,761 --> 00:04:28,301
but it'll be closed throughout September for refurbishment.

109
00:04:28,301 --> 00:04:29,186
I'm afraid.

110
00:04:29,186 --> 00:04:33,612
The gym will be available, though, at no extra charge.

111
00:04:33,612 --> 00:04:38,480
That's open all day, from six in the morning until midnight.

112
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,745
SAM:

113
00:04:39,745 --> 00:04:41,010
Right.

114
00:04:41,010 --> 00:04:41,395
ANDREW:

115
00:04:41,395 --> 00:04:42,936
And the tennis courts,

116
00:04:42,936 --> 00:04:46,402
but there is a small additional payment for those.

117
00:04:46,402 --> 00:04:47,942
We have four courts,

118
00:04:47,942 --> 00:04:53,334
and it's worth booking in advance if you possibly can, as there can be

119
00:04:53,334 --> 00:04:56,030
quite a long waiting list for them.

120
00:04:56,030 --> 00:04:56,607
SAM:

121
00:04:56,607 --> 00:04:57,183
Right.

122
00:04:57,183 --> 00:05:00,643
Now could we discuss the food?

123
00:05:00,643 --> 00:05:04,680
This would be dinner, around seven o'clock…
